{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25599736",
      "title": "Introducing Error Boundaries",
      "sourceHash": "fe5f2df67f1caa88e35881bf53152f7b9901540e1ab5647f5d7fc29eea68c0f7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 5.98,
          "en": "Let me introduce you to error boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.98,
          "end": 9.82,
          "en": "Sometimes something goes wrong in your applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.82,
          "end": 11.55,
          "en": "And I'm not talking about bugs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.55,
          "end": 13.54,
          "en": "you introduced as a developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.54,
          "end": 15.41,
          "en": "Of course, you should simply fix them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.41,
          "end": 18.79,
          "en": "but sometimes there are errors which you can't prevent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.79,
          "end": 22.66,
          "en": "or which are simply being used to transport information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.66,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "that something went wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 27.073,
          "en": "from one part of the application to another part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 31.09,
          "en": "Consider an HTTP request which is being sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.09,
          "end": 34.65,
          "en": "If the server is temporarily not responding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.65,
          "end": 37.01,
          "en": "the request can't complete",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.01,
          "end": 41.02,
          "en": "and you will likely end up with an error being generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.02,
          "end": 42.71,
          "en": "in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.71,
          "end": 45.92,
          "en": "Now, there is nothing you can do about that as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.92,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "servers can be offline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 52.1,
          "en": "And there are in general, errors which can't be prevented.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.1,
          "end": 55.55,
          "en": "Here, I built a little dummy example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.55,
          "end": 57.65,
          "en": "In the users component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.65,
          "end": 61.28,
          "en": "I added the component that update lifecycle method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.28,
          "end": 64.63,
          "en": "and in there I check if my users prop, which I'm getting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.63,
          "end": 66.16,
          "en": "which is an array of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.16,
          "end": 68.23,
          "en": "has a length of zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.23,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "which means there are no users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 74.48,
          "en": "In which case, I throw a new error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.48,
          "end": 78.09,
          "en": "And that is, of course, a technical thing in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 80.87,
          "en": "By doing this, by executing this line,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.87,
          "end": 83.08,
          "en": "I'm generating an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.08,
          "end": 86.8,
          "en": "and I let this error bubble up the call stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.8,
          "end": 89.81,
          "en": "So I pass it through all these components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.81,
          "end": 91.81,
          "en": "and if it's not handled anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.81,
          "end": 94.45,
          "en": "this will crash my application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.45,
          "end": 97.03999999999999,
          "en": "And you can see this if you add this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.03999999999999,
          "end": 99.58,
          "en": "if you run your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.58,
          "end": 102.95,
          "en": "As long as there are users, everything is fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.95,
          "end": 104.74000000000001,
          "en": "but if I search for something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.74000000000001,
          "end": 108.11,
          "en": "which is not part of any username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.11,
          "end": 109.3,
          "en": "like in S,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.3,
          "end": 111.43,
          "en": "this will crash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.43,
          "end": 114.56,
          "en": "And it crashes with the error I specified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.56,
          "end": 118.46000000000001,
          "en": "because it's my error which is not being handled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.46000000000001,
          "end": 121.38,
          "en": "Now, of course I could just simply not throw an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.38,
          "end": 123.94,
          "en": "but instead handle this case differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.94,
          "end": 126.5,
          "en": "but it's also quite common to use errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.5,
          "end": 128.42,
          "en": "not as a bad thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.42,
          "end": 131.78,
          "en": "but simply as a way of transporting the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.78,
          "end": 133.25,
          "en": "that something went wrong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.25,
          "end": 136.95,
          "en": "from place A to place B in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.95,
          "end": 139.21,
          "en": "You can learn more about that, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.21,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "learn more about embracing errors in my clean code course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 144.49,
          "en": "if you want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.49,
          "end": 145.89,
          "en": "but that's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.73,
          "end": 151.32999999999998,
          "en": "So here I generate an error and I want to generate an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.32999999999998,
          "end": 154.67000000000002,
          "en": "Of course, I don't want the entire application to crush,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.67000000000002,
          "end": 156.59,
          "en": "so what can we do?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 156.59,
          "end": 159.38,
          "en": "In regular JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.38,
          "end": 162.56,
          "en": "we use, try, catch for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.56,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "We can try some code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 167.56,
          "en": "which might fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.56,
          "end": 172.01,
          "en": "and we catch potential errors when that code executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.01,
          "end": 175.643,
          "en": "to then handle that error and run alternative code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.54,
          "end": 178.52,
          "en": "That's what we can do in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.52,
          "end": 180.01,
          "en": "And with react, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.01,
          "end": 183.4,
          "en": "we are just writing JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 183.4,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "Nonetheless, if an error is generated inside of a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.93,
          "end": 192.41,
          "en": "and we can't handle it in that component though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.41,
          "end": 194.94,
          "en": "let's say we don't wanna handle this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.94,
          "end": 196.45,
          "en": "in the users component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.45,
          "end": 198.8,
          "en": "but in a parent component, instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.8,
          "end": 201.35,
          "en": "then we can't use try, catch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 201.35,
          "end": 203.71,
          "en": "because that only works in places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 203.71,
          "end": 207.49,
          "en": "where we write regular JavaScript statements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207.49,
          "end": 209.9,
          "en": "and if we throw an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 209.9,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "and we wanna handle it in a parent component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 215.79,
          "en": "our problem is that in this case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.79,
          "end": 218.77,
          "en": "the users component is generating that error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 218.77,
          "end": 222.41,
          "en": "but that is not a regular JavaScript statement here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 222.41,
          "end": 226.36,
          "en": "Instead here, we have JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.36,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "and the error is generated inside of that JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 232.163,
          "en": "inside of the users component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.09,
          "end": 237.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, we can't wrap this JSX code with try, catch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 237.57999999999998,
          "end": 240.18,
          "en": "Something like this doesn't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.18,
          "end": 241.96,
          "en": "so that's not an option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.96,
          "end": 243.79,
          "en": "Instead in such a case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.79,
          "end": 247.71,
          "en": "you can build and utilize an error boundary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 247.71,
          "end": 249.95,
          "en": "and that's what we're going to do now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.95,
          "end": 252.1,
          "en": "For this, I'll add a new component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 252.1,
          "end": 255.57,
          "en": "and I will name it error boundary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.57,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "though the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 259.053,
          "en": "it doesn't have to be named like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 259.96,
          "end": 261.52,
          "en": "It's a JavaScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.52,
          "end": 264.61,
          "en": "and in there I will create a regular component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 264.61,
          "end": 267.16,
          "en": "which I'll name error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.16,
          "end": 271,
          "en": "So let's import component from react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 271,
          "end": 273.87,
          "en": "because I will build it as a class-based component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.87,
          "end": 277.36,
          "en": "as you can already tell, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.36,
          "end": 280.86,
          "en": "And now in there, I'll do something special.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 283.12,
          "en": "The error boundary component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.12,
          "end": 285.55,
          "en": "is a regular class-based component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 285.55,
          "end": 287.62,
          "en": "but it is a class-based component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 287.62,
          "end": 292.063,
          "en": "which implements the componentDidCatch lifecycle method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 294.99,
          "end": 298.89,
          "en": "The componentDidCatch lifecycle method can be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.89,
          "end": 301.62,
          "en": "to any class-based component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 301.62,
          "end": 304.94,
          "en": "and whenever you do add it to a class-based component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 304.94,
          "end": 308.55,
          "en": "it makes that class-based component an error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.55,
          "end": 311.97,
          "en": "It's just a term which we use to refer to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 311.97,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "when we talk about components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 316.27,
          "en": "that have this lifecycle method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 316.27,
          "end": 319.67,
          "en": "You can't edit two functional components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 319.67,
          "end": 323.21,
          "en": "and there is no equivalent for functional components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 323.21,
          "end": 324.62,
          "en": "at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 324.62,
          "end": 326.61,
          "en": "So if you wanna build an error boundary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.61,
          "end": 328.66,
          "en": "it needs to be a class-based component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 328.66,
          "end": 330.81,
          "en": "and then it is a class-based component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 330.81,
          "end": 333.82,
          "en": "which implements this lifecycle method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 333.82,
          "end": 337.24,
          "en": "Now, what's this special thing about this lifecycle method?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 337.24,
          "end": 340.03,
          "en": "Well, this lifecycle method will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 340.03,
          "end": 344.13,
          "en": "whenever one of the child components throws an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 344.13,
          "end": 346.17,
          "en": "or generates an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 346.17,
          "end": 349.33,
          "en": "Therefore, what we do in the error boundary as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 349.33,
          "end": 352.46,
          "en": "is we add a render method, like an all components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 352.46,
          "end": 355.57,
          "en": "and we return this props children,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 355.57,
          "end": 357.29,
          "en": "and that's special now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 357.29,
          "end": 360.87,
          "en": "Here I return this props children",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 360.87,
          "end": 364.89,
          "en": "because I want to wrap my error boundary component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 364.89,
          "end": 366.57,
          "en": "around components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 366.57,
          "end": 371.09,
          "en": "which should be protected by that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 371.09,
          "end": 373.57,
          "en": "So here, for example, in the user finder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 373.57,
          "end": 378.57,
          "en": "I could wrap the error boundary around my users component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 380.88,
          "end": 383.21,
          "en": "Of course, we now need to import it also.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 383.21,
          "end": 387.653,
          "en": "So we import error boundary from error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 388.81,
          "end": 391.92,
          "en": "And then we wrap it around any components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 391.92,
          "end": 395.90999999999997,
          "en": "which might throw errors which we wanna handle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 395.90999999999997,
          "end": 397.59000000000003,
          "en": "And of course, you can wrap it around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 397.59000000000003,
          "end": 398.93,
          "en": "more than one component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 398.93,
          "end": 400.423,
